### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?

With `slotAssignment: "manual"`, `slot.assign()` sets assigned nodes in dev-assigned order, so rendering and the accessibility tree follow that order. Sequential focus navigation orders a slot's scope in "shadow-including tree order" ([tabindex](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#attr-tabindex)), which is the host's child order. When the two differ, Tab order no longer matches visual or reading order (WCAG 2.4.3).

```html
<input id=before>
<div id=host>
  <input id=a>
  <input id=b>
  <input id=c>
</div>
<input id=after>
<script>
  const root = host.attachShadow({ mode: "open", slotAssignment: "manual" });
  root.innerHTML = "<slot></slot>";
  root.querySelector("slot").assign(c, a, b);
</script>
```

All engines render (and expose via the accessibility tree) C, A, B. 

However, the Tab order is inconsistent:

- Firefox: C, A, B (assigned order)
- Chromium: A, B, C (tree/light-dom order)
- WebKit: C, then leaves the host; Shift+Tab gives B, A. It mixes both orders and skips elements.

I think it makes sense to align that the Tab order should match the rendered and a11y tree order, but also wasn't sure if this required a specification update to be explicit about that or if it's just something that should be considered a bug.

Below I include a proposed WPT to validate this behavior, if it's aligned: 

<details>
<summary>Proposed WPT</summary>

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Sequential focus navigation with manually assigned slottables</title>
<link rel="help" href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#tabindex-ordered-focus-navigation-scope">
<link rel="help" href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#dom-slot-assign">
<script src="/resources/testharness.js"></script>
<script src="/resources/testharnessreport.js"></script>
<script src="/resources/testdriver.js"></script>
<script src="/resources/testdriver-vendor.js"></script>
<script src="/resources/testdriver-actions.js"></script>
<script src="resources/shadow-dom.js"></script>
<script src="resources/focus-utils.js"></script>

<input id="before">
<div id="host">
  <input id="a">
  <input id="b">
  <input id="c">
</div>
<input id="after">

<script>
'use strict';

const host = document.getElementById('host');
const root = host.attachShadow({ mode: 'open', slotAssignment: 'manual' });
root.innerHTML = '<slot></slot>';
root.querySelector('slot').assign(
  document.getElementById('c'),
  document.getElementById('a'),
  document.getElementById('b'));

async function sequence(startId, navigate) {
  document.getElementById(startId).focus();
  const ids = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    await navigate();
    ids.push(document.activeElement.id);
  }
  return ids;
}

promise_test(async () => {
  const forward = await sequence('before', navigateFocusForward);
  const backward = await sequence('after', navigateFocusBackward);
  assert_array_equals(forward.slice(0, 3).sort(), ['a', 'b', 'c'],
                      'Tab reaches every slotted input before leaving the host');
  assert_equals(forward[3], 'after');
  assert_array_equals(backward, [...forward.slice(0, 3)].reverse().concat('before'),
                      'Shift+Tab visits the same inputs in reverse');
}, 'Sequential focus navigation reaches every manually assigned slottable in both directions');

promise_test(async () => {
  await assert_focus_navigation_bidirectional(['before', 'c', 'a', 'b', 'after']);
}, 'Sequential focus navigation follows the order passed to slot.assign()');
</script>
```

</details>
